      "widgets_values": [
        "cinematic still of the interior of a decaying gothic manor, lit only by dozens of candles and a large open stone fireplace with burning logs. Warm flickering candlelight on rough stone walls, cobwebs, peeling plaster, heavy velvet drapes. No electric lighting. Sensual, conspiratorial atmosphere.\n\nThe man sits leaning back in an antique carved chair, relaxed, in a white shirt with the tie loosened and black suit trousers. His head is turned to his left and his eyes are fixed on the blonde woman, not on the viewer.\n\nThe blonde woman is draped across the arm of his chair and against his shoulder, in a revealing dark blue gown with a leg showing through the slit, straight blonde hair. Her face is turned away from the camera, in profile, looking up toward the brunette behind the chair, mid-conversation, lips slightly parted.\n\nThe brunette stands behind the chair, leaning on its high back with one forearm, looking down at the blonde, speaking to her. Her gaze is directed at the blonde's face.\n\nshot on Panasonic VariCam 35, ultra-smooth 180-degree shutter, shallow depth of field, Hammer Horror film aesthetic, Eastmancolor film stock, warm pushed saturation, slightly overexposed highlights, deep crushed shadows, lush theatrical lighting, gothic British period atmosphere, 1960s-1970s Bray Studios production design, velvet textures and rich decay, soft focus on backgrounds, cinematic 21:9 Ultrawide, smooth filmic motion, no digital sharpness, organic grain structure"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
